GazLang - a scripting language for web servers and command line tools
Usage: gaz [options] [file | -] [program arguments...]
  Runs the file, with everything after it as the program's arguments (args()).
  - reads the program from standard input, as no file does when something is piped.
Options:
  -h, --help     Show this help message
  -v, --version  Show version information
  -c, --code     Print the compiled bytecode instead of running it (gaz -c x.gaz > x.gzb)
  -t, --tokens   Print the lexer's tokens, one LINE TYPE VALUE per line, instead of interpreting
      --ast      Print the parser's tree instead of running it
  -f, --file     The file to run, as giving it first does
